From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: select WAN MTU field from hardware WAN slot

AN7581 has independent WAN0 and WAN1 MTU fields in REG_WAN_MTU0. The
existing driver always updates WAN_MTU0 because it historically supports a
single hardware WAN.

Use the per-netdev hardware WAN slot introduced by the multi-WAN preparation
patch to update the matching MTU field. This deliberately keys off the
hardware slot rather than the legacy LAN/WAN flag so a direct-PPE WAN1 can
coexist with a LAN sibling on the same GDM without migrating the whole GDM
to the legacy loopback/QDMA1 path.

Existing WAN0 behaviour remains unchanged.

---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2109,12 +2109,15 @@ static void airoha_dev_set_mtu(struct net_device *netdev)
 {
 	struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev = netdev_priv(netdev);
+	u32 mask;
 
 	airoha_ppe_set_mtu(dev);
-	if (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev))
-		airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_WAN_MTU0,
-			      WAN_MTU0_MASK,
-			      FIELD_PREP(WAN_MTU0_MASK, netdev->mtu));
+	if (dev->hw_wan_slot == AIROHA_HW_WAN_NONE)
+		return;
+
+	mask = dev->hw_wan_slot == AIROHA_HW_WAN1 ?
+		WAN_MTU1_MASK : WAN_MTU0_MASK;
+	airoha_fe_rmw(dev->eth, REG_WAN_MTU0, mask,
+		      __field_prep(mask, netdev->mtu));
 }
 
 static int airoha_dev_open(struct net_device *netdev)
